      "oslawRightsOverview": "Consumer contracts often include cooling-off periods for distance sales, and chargeback or cancellation rights may apply depending on how you paid and what you bought. Open guidance describes when you can cancel, what refunds are due, and how to escalate if a trader refuses.",
      "oslawRightsBullets": [
        {
          "text": "Distance / online purchases may have a statutory cooling-off period for many goods and services.",
          "sourceUrl": "https://www.citizensadvice.org.uk/consumer/changed-your-mind/cancel-something-being-paid-for-on-hire-purchase/",
          "sourceTitle": "Cancel something you bought on hire purchase - Citizens Advice"
        },
        {
          "text": "If a trader refuses a refund you believe you are owed, open guidance covers written complaints and ADR routes.",
          "sourceUrl": "https://www.citizensadvice.org.uk/consumer/changed-your-mind/cancel-something-being-paid-for-on-hire-purchase/",
          "sourceTitle": "Cancel something you bought on hire purchase - Citizens Advice"
        },
        {
          "text": "Card chargebacks and Section 75 claims may be options for certain card payments — check eligibility in open sources.",
          "sourceUrl": "https://www.citizensadvice.org.uk/consumer/changed-your-mind/cancel-something-being-paid-for-on-hire-purchase/",
          "sourceTitle": "Cancel something you bought on hire purchase - Citizens Advice"
        }
      ],
      "oslawSteps": [
        {
          "id": "cooling-off",
          "label": "Check if a cooling-off period applies",
          "detail": "Distance and online sales often have cancellation windows — open guidance explains exceptions.",
